==============================================================================
REASSEMBLED TELEMETRY LOG — v2.7.0
==============================================================================
This log was RE-ASSEMBLED after the fact, not emitted by a live batch run,
so the Speed Telemetry pipeline has an input to render this version's chart.

Why: the batch was scanned with a parallel driver that discarded galaxyscope's
per-repo telemetry (stdout), and the interim batch_scan_master logs were removed.
The engine does not persist per-repo scan time/rate in its artifacts, so the
table below could not be recovered from the outputs alone.

Reassembled from:
  - per-repo LOC : 'Total LOC' in each v2.7.0/<repo>/<repo>_galaxy_llm.md (exact).
  - per-repo time: '✅ <repo> (<n>s)' wall times in reassembly_source_parallel_run.log.

CAVEAT: times were measured under 2-way worker concurrency, so they are
wall times, not single-process engine time — the derived LOC/s is ~1/2 of the
engine's true throughput and is a LOWER BOUND. NOT directly comparable to the
sequentially-measured v2.4.6/v2.4.7 batches. For a clean, comparable chart, re-run
the sequential batch_process_restored.py (it emits this log natively).
Coverage: 513 repos with per-repo timing reassembled; 169 omitted.
